# Line-ending policy.
#
# The documentation hash gate (cmake/check_doc_hashes.cmake, registered as the
# `doc_hashes` ctest entry) records the SHA256 of the committed bytes, which are
# LF. GitHub's windows-latest image sets core.autocrlf=true in git's system
# config, so a plain checkout rewrites every .md to CRLF and all 24 recorded
# hashes drift at once (first seen in the MSVC CI run of 2026-11-05). Pinning
# eol=lf makes checkouts byte-identical on every platform, so a recorded hash
# still equals `sha256sum` of the file on disk.
#
# No tracked file contains CR, so adding this needs no renormalization commit.

# Text: LF in the repository and in every working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must stay LF even if a Windows editor rewrites them: bash and
# MSYS refuse to run a CRLF script (bad interpreter).
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary: never touch the bytes. Declared explicitly because `eol=` implies
# "text", which would corrupt these on commit.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.qlc binary
*.qla binary
*.a binary
*.o binary
*.obj binary
*.lib binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.zip binary
